{"id": "f0292075-0734-482d-83ed-bdf7e7a7a3d9", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll break down your CloudTrail charges by usage type, comparing this month so far with last month, and check how your trails are configured. A cost increase with no new trails usually comes from data events, extra management-event copies, or CloudTrail Lake ingestion.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_piDLx0taO7ZHunHXeJkmGa", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cloudtrail-cost-breakdown", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Explain why the AWS CloudTrail bill roughly doubled this month even though no new trails were added. Produce a concise, evidence-based breakdown of where the increase comes from.",
  "context": "User sees CloudTrail charges about 2x higher in the current month (November 2026, month-to-date through 2026-11-19) than before. They say they did not add trails. This is a cost question. Account: 012345678901 (agent space account; also check other associated accounts if cost is consolidated at a payer level and visible). Use Cost Explorer (us-east-1 endpoint) read-only calls.",
  "resources": ["AWS CloudTrail service charges", "account 012345678901"],
  "timeframe": "Current month 2026-11-01 to 2026-11-19 vs. prior month 2026-10-01 to 2026-11-01 (also compare same number of days, and look at daily granularity for the last 60 days to find when the jump started)",
  "criteria": "1) Cost Explorer: CloudTrail cost grouped by USAGE_TYPE (and by LINKED_ACCOUNT and REGION) for both periods, with daily trend to locate the date the increase began. Distinguish management events (additional copies beyond the first free copy), data events (S3/Lambda/DynamoDB etc.), Insights events, network activity events, and CloudTrail Lake ingestion/storage/query. 2) Describe current trails in all regions (describe_trails with includeShadowTrails, get_trail_status, get_event_selectors / advanced event selectors, get_insight_selectors), and list CloudTrail Lake event data stores. Look for: multiple trails logging management events in the same region, organization trails also creating copies, data events enabled on high-volume buckets/functions/tables, Insights enabled, multi-region trails. 3) Use CloudTrail lookup of management events to see whether anyone recently called PutEventSelectors, PutInsightSelectors, CreateTrail, UpdateTrail, CreateEventDataStore, or StartLogging around when the cost jump began. 4) Also note if a recent increase in underlying API/S3 activity volume could explain data event cost. Give a ranked list of the likely drivers with dollar amounts and evidence, and suggest where to dig deeper. Do not make any changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Analyze CloudTrail cost by usage type and trail configuration"}], "created_at": null}

